      "widgets_values": [
        "This is Hot Lazy Switch: plug in up to 10 things, name them, and pick which one actually flows through the output from the index dropdown. Only the one you pick runs — everything else stays disconnected, so it doesn't even load.\n\nThe three Text nodes here are just stand-ins so this workflow opens and runs for anyone, no matter what models or images they've got installed. To use it for real:\n\nUnplug a Text node and wire in whatever you actually want to switch between.\nCheckpoints, LoRAs, images, prompts, conditioning, anything. \n\nFirst thing you connect decides the type for the whole node — all the slots you use need to match that type, since it's really one shared connection wearing different clothes.\n\nType something into the matching name_0 / name_1 / name_2 box so the index dropdown shows a real name instead of \"Input 1\", \"Input 2\".\n\nKeep plugging things in one at a time — a fresh empty socket shows up each time you fill the last one, up to 10 total.\n\nSet index to whichever name you want live right now.\n\nDelete this note once you're familiar with this mechanic."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "This is Hot Lazy Switch: plug in up to 10 things, name them, and pick which one actually flows through the output from the index dropdown. Only the one you pick runs — everything else stays disconnected, so it doesn't even load.\n\nThe three Text nodes here are just stand-ins so this workflow opens and runs for anyone, no matter what models or images they've got installed. To use it for real:\n\nUnplug a Text node and wire in whatever you actually want to switch between.\nCheckpoints, LoRAs, images, prompts, conditioning, anything. \n\nFirst thing you connect decides the type for the whole node — all the slots you use need to match that type, since it's really one shared connection wearing different clothes.\n\nType something into the matching name_0 / name_1 / name_2 box so the index dropdown shows a real name instead of \"Input 1\", \"Input 2\".\n\nKeep plugging things in one at a time — a fresh empty socket shows up each time you fill the last one, up to 10 total.\n\nSet index to whichever name you want live right now.\n\nDelete this note once you're familiar with this mechanic."
      },
